              {
                "text": "**Analyzing Grid Structures**\n\nI'm currently focused on the challenge of color-coding grids containing 5s and 0s. I'm starting by examining the first training input and trying to analyze the connected components formed by the 5s, considering whether to use 8-way or 4-way connectivity. I've begun to look at the first row.\n\n\n**Mapping Component Sizes**\n\nI've been analyzing the component sizes in the training data, noting the sizes of connected '5' components. I think I see a pattern: the size of a component is mapped to a color, potentially inverted. I'm seeing if size 1 maps to color 5, size 2 maps to color 3, size 3 maps to color 2, size 4 maps to color 1, and size 5 maps to color 5. I will check training data 2 for verification!\n\n\n",
